SPD repository licensing
========================

This repository uses an explicit split license.

Software and code
-----------------

Source code, scripts, validators, test programs, build configuration, and CI
configuration are licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(SPDX: Apache-2.0):

https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

This scope includes code under `harness/`, `mapping/`, `renderers/`, `scripts/`,
`semantic_pdf/`, `validation/`, `validator-a/`, and `validator-b/`; Python test
programs under `tests/`; and repository automation under `.github/`.

Specification and documentation
-------------------------------

The SPD specification, prose documentation, schemas, reports, conformance
fixtures, and other non-code research material are licensed under the Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International license (SPDX: CC-BY-4.0):

https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

This scope includes `spec/`, `docs/`, `schemas/`, `reports/`, the root Markdown
documents, the conformance packages and expected results under `tests/`, and
research material under `corpus/` and `benchmarks/`, except for source-code files
covered by Apache-2.0 above.

Attribution may be given as: “Semantic Portable Document (SPD) contributors.”
When redistributing modified documentation, indicate that changes were made and
link to the source repository where practical.

Third-party material
--------------------

Third-party components and test assets, if any, remain subject to their own
licenses and notices. No license in this file grants rights to third-party marks.

Unless a file or directory states otherwise, the scope rules above control.
Contributors retain copyright in their contributions and license them under the
applicable terms when contributing.
